id: pm-ed28wi
title: "Linked-test commands are merge-unioned workspace data executed with shell:true — no provenance, allowlist, or confirmation boundary"
description: "Linked test commands are arbitrary shell strings stored in item data and executed without any trust boundary. src/sdk/test/execution.ts createLinkedTestChild spawns the stored command with shell:true, cwd process.cwd(), detached on POSIX, inheriting the caller's environment; there is no allowlist, no confirmation prompt, no dry-run default, and no provenance check anywhere in that path or in src/cli/commands/test.ts. The exposure is created by the merge model this project deliberately adopted: docs/MERGE_SAFETY.md specifies that append-like item collections merge by set union, so a linked test added on another branch is silently unioned into the item on merge, and the merge drivers are installed repo-wide by pm merge install. A maintainer or agent who then runs 'pm test <id> --run' or 'pm test-all' executes whatever command arrived with that merge. Every documented multi-agent workflow in this repo — fleet lanes, worktree agents, branch merges — routes through exactly that sequence. Duplicate check: searched linked test/shell/untrusted/trust boundary all-status. pm-g072 (closed) hardened untrusted dependency specs reaching npm install during extension install, a different input path; pm-pim7 owns secret guarding; pm-u14c owns author authenticity and pm-xc68 policy roles, both about who wrote a mutation rather than what executing stored data is allowed to do; pm-3z0k owns detached attestation. No item owns execution trust for linked test commands."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 1
tags[6]: "area:test",concurrency,merge-safety,multi-agent,security,trust
created_at: "2026-07-25T07:11:20.321Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-22T22:49:55.425Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-22T22:49:54.860Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-22T22:49:54.860Z"
author: unknown
estimated_minutes: 480
acceptance_criteria: "A documented trust boundary governs linked-test execution: pm records provenance for every linked test command (author, source branch or merge origin, and whether it arrived through a merge rather than a local mutation); executing a command whose provenance is not locally trusted requires an explicit opt-in (config policy plus an explicit flag) instead of running silently; pm validate or pm health surfaces linked test commands that changed through a merge since the last local acknowledgment; docs/TESTING.md and docs/MERGE_SAFETY.md state the boundary and the threat model explicitly; the default behaviour for a workspace whose items were only mutated locally is unchanged so no existing workflow regresses; regression tests cover merge-introduced commands, the opt-in path, and the refusal path"
goal: project management = context management
objective: Make stored-then-executed workspace data safe under the multi-agent merge model pm is designed for
value: "pm's core promise is that many agents merge tracker state across branches without conflict; execution of merged data must not be a silent code-execution path, or the merge model becomes the attack surface"
why_now: "The merge-safety wave shipped and pm merge install is now standard bootstrap; pm-76dnfg is building randomized N-branch merge conformance, which is exactly the point to state what merged execution data is allowed to do"
parent: pm-qwoy
risk: high
confidence: high
release: v2026.8.23
severity: high
environment: src/sdk/test/execution.ts createLinkedTestChild; docs/MERGE_SAFETY.md set-union semantics for append-like collections; .gitattributes pm-item-toon/pm-item-markdown drivers
repro_steps: "Branch A adds a linked test to an item via pm test <id> --add; merge branch A into branch B where the pm merge drivers are installed; the command is unioned into the item on B; running pm test <id> --run on B executes it with shell:true and the caller's environment"
resolution: Completed fail-closed linked-command provenance and merge trust enforcement across SDK execution and CLI adapters.
expected_result: "Malformed, legacy, or merge-introduced commands remain untrusted until explicit clone-local acknowledgement or dual-consent execution policy; acknowledgement never executes commands."
actual_result: "Invalid provenance no longer normalizes to legacy trust, merge union marks legacy commands untrusted, background acknowledgement is refused, and trust/security gates pass."
fixed_version: 2026.8.23
