comments[5]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-25T07:13:02.239Z","harness:claude-code","Duplicate-check evidence (all-status pm search over linked test, shell, untrusted, trust boundary, execution): matched closed pm-g072, pm-swie, pm-7v9s, pm-2kkl and open pm-qwoy, pm-pim7, pm-u14c, pm-xc68, pm-3z0k. pm-g072 hardened a different untrusted input path (manifest dependency specs reaching npm install); the identity items govern who authored a mutation, not what executing stored data may do. No item owns execution trust for linked test commands. Filed as a child of pm-qwoy."
  "2026-07-25T07:13:03.156Z","harness:claude-code","Code evidence: src/sdk/test/execution.ts createLinkedTestChild calls spawn(command, { cwd: process.cwd(), env, shell: true, windowsHide: true, detached: process.platform !== 'win32' }). A grep for allowlist, allowList, confirm, --yes, trusted or sanitiz across src/sdk/test/execution.ts and src/cli/commands/test.ts returns nothing, so no guard exists on that path. docs/TESTING.md mentions shell syntax only as an authoring convenience and docs/MERGE_SAFETY.md documents that append-like item collections merge by set union — which is the mechanism that lets a linked test authored on one branch appear on another without a local mutation. The repo's own bootstrap instructs every clone to run 'pm merge install', so the union semantics are active by default in exactly the multi-agent branch workflows this project targets."
  "2026-08-22T16:34:37.883Z","harness:codex","Implementation start 2026-08-22: actively implementing provenance, local acknowledgment, merge-introduced command refusal, explicit opt-in, validation/health visibility, and documented threat-model behavior in the same SDK-first linked-test tranche as pm-e97jyf and pm-efkvdy."
  "2026-08-22T18:26:48.844Z","harness:codex","Verification evidence 2026-08-22: every newly linked command records immutable author/time/local-or-merge/source-ref provenance; merge-unioned commands are marked untrusted; execution fails closed unless project policy and the per-run flag both consent; clone-local fingerprint acknowledgment is separate from execution; validation reports unacknowledged commands. Focused trust/merge/config/validation tests, manual foreign-branch proof, pnpm audit, repository secret scan, and GitHub Dependabot/code/secret inventories all passed or reported zero alerts. Full suite passed 7,794 tests at exact 100/100/100/100."
  "2026-08-22T22:49:43.544Z","harness:codex","Final continuation evidence 2026-08-23: malformed or missing provenance now fails closed instead of inheriting legacy trust, merge-unioned legacy commands are explicitly marked untrusted, and clone acknowledgement is a foreground-only non-executing operation. Linked trust/config/validation tests passed 169/169; pnpm audit reported no vulnerabilities, the secret scan found none, and GitHub Dependabot, code-scanning, and secret-scanning open-alert inventories were empty."
